WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
This is lesson four, XML layouts — pointer P2. We stay inside this pointer: layout
attributes, ConstraintLayout, and merge plus include from the study guide, pages 107 and 108.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:28.320
I'll show the real slides and the study guide, write the XML on a board, then build a real app on
a real emulator. We'll break four layouts, fix them, and finish with two exam-style TODO questions.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:34.272
Aim for the paper on Tuesday the
24th of November, Lab 1, 9 o'clock.

00:00:34.272 --> 00:00:51.672
Here is the UI Architecture slide on the layout types. FrameLayout stacks children in one corner. LinearLayout
is a row or a column. RelativeLayout places a child relative to the parent or a sibling. GridLayout is a table.

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:57.072
The exam will name these, and it will ask you
for the attributes that place the children.

00:00:57.072 --> 00:01:03.648
Match parent means fill the parent. Wrap
content means shrink to the widget's own size.

00:01:03.648 --> 00:01:18.912
Padding is space inside a view; margin is space outside it. Sizes in layouts use dp, so they stay the
same physical size on different screens. Text uses sp, so it can follow the user's font-size setting.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:35.424
On EditText, the exam also likes inputType, hint, and imeOptions. inputType textEmailAddress or textPassword
changes the keyboard. hint is the grey placeholder. imeOptions actionNext moves to the next field.

00:01:35.424 --> 00:01:50.496
Study guide page 105. A vertical LinearLayout holds a horizontal one. That inner row has
padding of 5 dp, and two buttons. Each button has weight 1, so they share the row equally.

00:01:50.496 --> 00:02:02.856
The study guide writes fill parent plus weight. The cheatsheet and Sample
B write 0 dp plus weight. Both work. Write 0 dp — that is the current form.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:18.456
Same pages, RelativeLayout. The button bar uses layout_alignParentBottom, so it sits on the
bottom of the screen. The ListView uses layout_above the bar, and layout_alignParentLeft.

00:02:18.456 --> 00:02:28.224
The cheatsheet also has layout_alignParentStart,
layout_toEndOf, and layout_below — same idea, different names.

00:02:28.224 --> 00:02:40.848
One trap: a RelativeLayout question is not answered with a constraint attribute.
That's layout_alignParentBottom, not layout_constraintBottom_toBottomOf.

00:02:40.848 --> 00:02:55.272
ConstraintLayout, from the XML cheatsheet and from Sample B question 4. You pin a side of a view to
a side of the parent or another view. Width 0 dp means stretch between the start and end anchors.

00:02:55.272 --> 00:03:07.608
layout_constraintTop_toTopOf, Start_toStartOf, End_toEndOf,
Top_toBottomOf, Bottom_toBottomOf — learn those five names.

00:03:07.608 --> 00:03:28.584
Study guide pages 107 and 108, and UI Architecture slide 15. include pastes another layout file into this one. If that file's root
is merge, the merge tag is thrown away, and its children join the parent directly — no extra wrapper. That flattens the hierarchy.

00:03:28.584 --> 00:03:36.912
Do not call setContentView on a merge layout. Merge is
only valid when it is being included into a real parent.

00:03:36.912 --> 00:03:47.184
Here is UI Architecture slide 15. Flatten the hierarchy: keep
layouts under 10 levels, and use merge to erase a redundant root.

00:03:47.184 --> 00:03:54.144
ViewStub is on this slide too, but it is not on the
official pointer list, so we will not write it on the board.

00:03:54.144 --> 00:03:58.200
A horizontal LinearLayout
with padding 5 dp.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:08.490
Each button is width 0 dp, and layout_weight 1. They share
the leftover space equally, so List and Add are the same size.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:14.196
If you drop the weight and leave wrap content,
they shrink to the left and leave a gap.

00:04:14.646 --> 00:04:23.406
The list screen is a RelativeLayout. The title is
alignParentTop. The included bar is alignParentBottom.

00:04:23.856 --> 00:04:30.984
The items sit layout_above the bar,
layout_below the title, and alignParentLeft.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:35.874
Change the bar to alignParentTop,
and it covers the title.

00:04:36.324 --> 00:04:49.788
The form is ConstraintLayout. The name field is width 0 dp, top, start and end of the
parent — so it stretches full width under the top. Quantity is top_toBottomOf the name.

00:04:50.238 --> 00:04:55.158
Save is 0 dp, pinned to the
bottom of this ConstraintLayout.

00:04:55.608 --> 00:05:02.256
Miss those constraints, and the button jumps to
zero, zero — the top-left — and covers the title.

00:05:02.706 --> 00:05:11.778
header_banner.xml starts with merge, not a FrameLayout.
include it, and the two TextViews join the parent.

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:17.868
The bar file keeps a LinearLayout root,
because we need one view to pin to the bottom.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:28.662
Inflate a merge file with no parent, as if it were a screen, and you get InflateException:
merge can be used only with a valid ViewGroup root and attachToRoot true.

00:05:29.112 --> 00:05:45.504
This is the real project, Pantry Layouts. The add screen is a vertical LinearLayout: the merge banner, a ConstraintLayout
form, and the weighted bar. The list screen is the RelativeLayout we just wrote. Every line has a comment.

00:05:45.504 --> 00:06:02.088
Look at the constraints on the name field: width 0 dp, top, start and end of the parent. Quantity is top_toBottomOf
the name. Save is pinned to the bottom of this ConstraintLayout, full width, just above the included bar.

00:06:02.088 --> 00:06:20.712
This is header_banner.xml from the real project. The root is merge, not a FrameLayout. Two TextViews: the title and
a short subtitle. When activity_main includes this file, these two views join the vertical LinearLayout directly.

00:06:20.712 --> 00:06:38.160
And this is bar_actions.xml. A horizontal LinearLayout, padding 5 dp, two buttons, each 0 dp with weight 1.
This file keeps a real LinearLayout root, so the list screen can pin the whole bar to the bottom as one view.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:55.560
The list screen is a RelativeLayout. The title is alignParentTop. The included bar is alignParentBottom. The
items sit above the bar, below the title, and alignParentLeft. That is the study guide pattern, in a real file.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:01.464
Gradle assembleDebug — BUILD SUCCESSFUL,
on this machine, with the real project.

00:07:01.464 --> 00:07:12.336
And here it is on a real Pixel 6, API 34. I type Rice, 2,
pick Cups, tick Staple, hide the keyboard, and tap Save.

00:07:12.336 --> 00:07:18.840
The list shows Rice x 2 cups, staple, and the
List and Add buttons sit equal at the bottom.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:24.408
List and Add switch the two screens.
The same bar is included on both.

00:07:24.408 --> 00:07:36.192
Mistake one. I removed the constraint attributes from Save. No crash — the button
just sits at the top-left and covers the title. Constraints are not optional.

00:07:36.192 --> 00:07:41.328
Put them back, rebuild, and Save is
at the bottom again, full width.

00:07:41.328 --> 00:07:51.888
Mistake two. I took layout_weight off the List and Add buttons and left
wrap content. They no longer share the row; they shrink to the left.

00:07:51.888 --> 00:07:56.304
Put 0 dp and weight 1 back,
and they are equal again.

00:07:56.304 --> 00:08:06.864
Mistake three. I treated the merge banner as a screen: setContentView
of an inflate of header_banner with a null parent. The app stops.

00:08:06.864 --> 00:08:13.968
Logcat: InflateException, merge can be used only
with a valid ViewGroup root and attachToRoot true.

00:08:13.968 --> 00:08:23.160
A merge layout is not a screen. Point setContentView at
activity_main, which includes the banner, and it starts cleanly.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:32.784
Mistake four. On the list, I set the bar to alignParentTop,
and I dropped layout_above. The bar covers the title.

00:08:32.784 --> 00:08:40.440
Put alignParentBottom back, and layout_above on the
items, and the bar sits on the bottom where it belongs.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:54.072
Write these down. 0 dp plus weight shares a LinearLayout row. RelativeLayout uses
alignParentBottom, layout_above, alignParentLeft — not constraint attributes.

00:08:54.072 --> 00:09:05.304
ConstraintLayout needs anchors; 0 dp stretches between them. include
with merge throws the merge tag away. Do not setContentView a merge file.

00:09:05.304 --> 00:09:24.048
In the exam, name the attribute correctly for the layout you are in. RelativeLayout is layout_alignParentBottom,
layout_above, layout_alignParentLeft. ConstraintLayout is the constraint family, and 0 dp stretches between anchors.

00:09:24.048 --> 00:09:35.688
For a weighted row, write 0 dp and layout_weight. If you see include and merge,
remember merge is thrown away, and you must not setContentView that file.

00:09:35.688 --> 00:09:44.592
Write the ids carefully: a typo in layout_above or in a
constraint is a blank or overlapping screen, not a compile error.

00:09:44.592 --> 00:09:53.592
Your turn. Two questions, TODO style, like the CA. Pause,
write your XML, then I'll show the answers and a real run.

00:09:53.592 --> 00:10:08.304
Question 1 is CA Test question 2: a vertical LinearLayout login screen. Fill in the four
TODOs: orientation, the email EditText, the password EditText, and a Login button with ems 10.

00:10:28.304 --> 00:10:39.849
Question 2 is in the Smart Pantry Add Ingredient setting. It draws
on Sample B question 4 and the study guide, pages 107 and 108.

00:10:39.849 --> 00:10:48.801
Four TODOs: include the merge banner, constrain the name field,
pin Save to the bottom, and include the weighted bar as navbar.

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:24.833
Here are the answers. Question 1: orientation vertical; email is full width, wrap height, inputType
textEmailAddress, hint Email; password uses textPassword; the button is wrap content, ems 10, text Login.

00:11:24.833 --> 00:11:39.713
Question 2: include header_banner; the name field is width 0 dp with top, start and end of parent;
Save is 0 dp, bottom, start and end of the ConstraintLayout; include bar_actions as navbar.

00:11:39.713 --> 00:11:49.289
And a real run of those answers: the login screen, tap Login, and the
form we built — banner, fields, Save, and the equal List and Add bar.

00:11:49.289 --> 00:11:58.289
That's lesson four. Next is lesson five: the basics, more
layout attributes, and testing with boundary value analysis.

00:11:58.289 --> 00:12:06.113
Write the two questions on paper, run the project, and
send me photos of your work. See you in the next one.
